  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently working on an avatar (from scratch, not downloaded) and finally got it to a state where I wanted to start testing in-game.\n-Avatar was placed in the scene and all materials were applied using the basic Unity Standard shader.\n-No extra systems have been created.\n-Mesh import settings set to keep quads, with weld vertices disabled\n-blender reports the mesh as having a total of 53016 quads, I have manually verified that all faces in all meshes are quads\n-Unity reports the individual meshes as having triangle counts of 768, 2016, 10120, 84864, 6160, and 2104, this gives a total of 106032 tris, which matches the 53016 quads reported by blender\n-Unity's scene statistics reports 107.7K tris being rendered when lights are disabled, which again matches the expected count\nDespite all of the above, vrchat reports the avatar's polygon count as 70686, which neither correlates with the quad count (the expected value) or the triangle count.  I've spent days now trying to figure out how the SDK would possibly be coming up with this figure and cannot conceive of any explanation, and can only conclude that there must be a bug in how the SDK counts polygons\n\nI've thus far seen the same result in both sdk version 2022.04.26.15.46 and 2022.05.04.17.47",
